/-!
# Exact degree-seven modular-polynomial correspondence

The seven existing roots of the full candidate polynomial satisfy the literal
classical Phi_2 expression on exactly the certified seven-cycle. This upgrades
congruence edges modulo 433^4 to exact equations in the completed quadratic
order. The proof uses two explicit integer polynomial identities, simple-root
Hensel lifting, and uniqueness. It does not require the completion to be a domain.

This theorem does not identify the candidate polynomial analytically with a CM
class polynomial, identify Phi_2 with an isogeny correspondence, or construct the
arithmetic theta tower. Those arithmetic identifications remain separate.

The polynomial identities are regenerated by scripts/generate_horizontal71.py.
-/

noncomputable section

